    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Y1zBiwrAYWiD24zS6xVdwc)_\n\nFixes the errors seen when starting Emacs from `main`, and audits the other `use-package` forms.\n\n**Root causes**\n- `Cannot load goto-last-change / rainbow-mode / treemacs-nerd-icons / org-contrib / openwith`, and `ns-auto-titlebar/:init`: these forms had no `:ensure`. Elpaca's `use-package` support installs nothing by default; `elpaca-use-package-by-default` in `init.el` does not exist in current Elpaca (checked in its source). The `locate-library` guards removed in #61 used to hide this.\n- `Failed to parse package consult-snapfile ... sp-path`: `use-package` reads a list given to `:load-path` as a list of paths and evaluates each symbol as a variable. The path now goes through the constant `sp-consult-snapfile-dir`.\n- `which-key loaded before Elpaca activation`: the raw `(which-key-mode 1)` in `sp-keys` autoloaded the built-in package early. Removed; the existing `use-package which-key` enables the mode. The stray `(which-key-mode +1)` `:custom` entry is removed too.\n\n**Audit (second commit)**\n- All other third-party `use-package` forms without `:ensure` now have `:ensure t` (about 70). `inheritenv` used `:straight`, which this config does not use; `org-focus-hud` gets `(:host github :repo \"SSD2019/org-focus-hud\")`.\n- Left alone: `tramp`, `pulse`, `org` (built-in), `exwm` (module not loaded), `excali` (local checkout), `citar-org-node` (`:vc`).\n- Reordered so Elpaca does not queue a dependency first: `company` before `company-quickhelp`, `go-mode` before the Go helpers, `auctex` before `auctex-latexmk` and `company-auctex`.\n\nModule docs in `docs/tangles/` are updated and their code blocks match the `.el` files. CHANGELOG: one entry in \"Startup and module load order\" (after #61), and a duplicated `Fixed` entry removed.\n\n**Not tested** (no Emacs here): nothing was loaded or byte-compiled. `use-package` and Elpaca behaviour was read from their sources. I could not reach MELPA or GNU ELPA from the container, so I assumed the package names (for example `go-complete`, `dot-mode`, `pcomplete-extension`) exist there; an unknown name will show up as an Elpaca error on first start. Please start Emacs and check `*Messages*` and `M-x elpaca-log`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_012aF5fvrjTcBwiu2drDZnyx\n",
